coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder run [flags] <workspace> [command...]

  Run a workload in its own workspace daemon, provisioned at runtime

  Provision a new workspace daemon from the shape the workspace's template
  declares, without a workspace build. Each workload gets its own identity. The
  command, if any, is run by the new daemon and its output is streamed.
    - Start a workload and run a command in it:
  
       $ coder run my-workspace -- coder identity
  
    - List the workloads of a workspace:
  
       $ coder run --list my-workspace
  
    - Remove a workload:
  
       $ coder run --remove workload-1a2b3c4d my-workspace

OPTIONS:
  -c, --column [name|status|shape|requested by|identity|pod] (default: name,status,shape,requested by,identity)
          Columns to display in table output.

  -l, --list bool
          List the workspace's workloads instead of starting one.

      --name string
          A name for the workload. It becomes the name of its workspace agent.

      --no-wait bool
          Return as soon as the workload is requested, and print its ID.

  -o, --output table|json (default: table)
          Output format.

      --remove string
          Remove the named workload instead of starting one.

      --shape string
          The workload shape to clone, by agent name. Only needed when the
          template declares several.

      --timeout duration (default: 10m)
          How long to wait for the workload to start and its command to finish.

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
